==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[æquality]] {{qualifier|archaic}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|fro|en}} {{term|equalité|lang=fro}} (French {{term|égalité|lang=fr}}), from {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|aequālitās}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|US}} {{enPR|ĭʹkwŏl-ĭ-tē}} {{IPA|/ɪˈkwɒl.ɪ.ti/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~|equalities}}

# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The fact of being [[equal]].
# {{context|uncountable|mathematics|lang=en}} The fact of being equal, of having the same value.
# {{context|uncountable|lang=en}} The equal treatment of people irrespective of social or cultural differences.

====Synonyms====
* (''fact of being equal''): [[equivalence]] parity,

====Antonyms====
* (''fact of being equal''): [[difference]], [[inequality]]
* (''equal treatment of people''): [[discrimination]], [[inequality]] nonequivilence

